window.MONSTER_CHUNK_70 = [{"name":"Warden Robot","cr":9,"xp":6400,"alignment":"N","size":"Large","type":"construct","subtypes":["robot"],"init":8,"senses":[{"type":"blindsight","modifier":"30 ft."},{"type":"darkvision","modifier":"60 ft."},{"type":"low-light vision"}],"auras":["infrasonic field (30 ft., DC 17)"],"ac":23,"ac_touch":13,"ac_flat_footed":19,"ac_mods":"+4 Dex, +10 natural, -1 size","hp":112,"hd":"15d10+30","hdvalue":15,"fort":8,"ref":12,"will":10,"defensive_abilities":["all-around vision","hardness 10","reactive armor","resilient"],"immunities":["construct traits"],"weaknesses":["vulnerable to critical hits and electricity"],"speed":[{"type":"land","speed":30}],"melee":"2 slams +18 (1d8+4)","ranged":"2 integrated sonic disruptors +18 ranged touch (2d8 sonic)","space":"10 ft.","reach":"10 ft.","special_attacks":[{"type":"combined arms"},{"type":"dazzler"},{"type":"integrated sonic disruptor"}],"strength":18,"dexterity":19,"intelligence":11,"wisdom":14,"charisma":1,"baseatk":15,"cmb":20,"cmd":34,"feats":[{"feat":"Alertness"},{"feat":"Combat Reflexes"},{"feat":"Improved Initiative"},{"feat":"Nimble Moves"},{"feat":"Point-Blank Shot"},{"feat":"Power Attack"},{"feat":"Precise Shot"},{"feat":"Stand Still"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Climb","value":10},{"skill":"Perception","value":20},{"skill":"Sense Motive","value":16}],"languages":["Androffan"],"environments":["any (Numeria)"],"organizations":["solitary","pair","sentry (3-12)"],"treasure":"none","description_visual":"Crafted of a strange, dull metal, this bulky construct stomps forward on stout, multi-jointed legs.","group":"Robot","source":"AP 87","special_abilities":[{"type":"Combined Arms","kind":"Ex","details":"As part of a full-attack action, a warden robot can attack with both melee and ranged integrated weapons."},{"type":"Dazzler","kind":"Ex","details":"As a standard action, a warden robot can target a single creature with a beam of strobing light that functions as a gaze attack with a range of 60 ft. A creature subject to this attack must succeed at a DC 17 Fortitude save or be blinded for 2d4 rounds. Creatures that successfully save are dazzled for 1d4 rounds. Creatures with light blindness or light sensitivity take a -4 penalty on the saving throw. This is a light effect, and the save DC is Intelligence-based."},{"type":"Infrasonic Field","kind":"Ex","details":"Warden robots constantly emit powerful sound waves at a frequency below normal hearing. These vibrations can debilitate living beings within 30 ft. Such creatures must succeed at DC 17 Fortitude save or fall prone and be nauseated for 1d4 rounds. A warden robot can suppress or resume this ability as a free action. This is a sonic effect, and the save DC is Intelligence-based."},{"type":"Integrated Sonic Disruptor","kind":"Ex","details":"A warden robot's arms contain built-in ranged weapons that emit focused sound waves in 100-foot rays that deal 2d8 points of sonic damage."},{"type":"Reactive Armor","kind":"Ex","details":"A warden robot is covered in a special shell that reacts explosively to powerful strikes. Due to this covering, a warden robot gains light fortification (25% chance to negate critical hits and sneak attacks). When the armor negates a critical hit from a melee weapon, the attacker takes an amount of fire damage equal to half of the damage dealt to the robot. Attackers using reach or ranged weapons avoid this damage."},{"type":"Resilient","kind":"Ex","details":"Warden robots receive a +3 racial bonus on all saving throws."}],"description":"Wardens are dangerous guardian robots often found protecting sealed vaults or patrolling ancient, buried corridors. They carry out their orders with ruthlessness and zeal, usually offering no warning before attacking a perceived threat. The Technic League has had moderate success in controlling a few of these robots, and occasionally assigns them as guards for valuable treasures or important prisoners, roles for which they're well suited.\n\nAlthough the mere sight of these massive machines is imposing enough to ward off most intruders, those who are undeterred by a warden's appearance soon find the robot to be quite capable of destroying those who enter its territory without proper clearance. Unlike golems or similarly mindless constructs, wardens possess an intelligence that allows them to employ tactics, either on their own or as part of a unit. When acting in groups, the robots are smart enough to suppress and reactivate their nausea-inducing sound waves in concert, maximizing the length of time their opponents are incapacitated.\n\nMost wardens are in Silver Mount, but some can be found in many other parts of Numeria. Nearly all share the same characteristics: a squat upper body with a domed shape and two arms ending in six surprisingly dexterous \"fingers\" surrounding emitters that serve as its primary ranged weapons. Two stout, multi-jointed legs provide the construct with great mobility, even on hilly or rough terrain.\n\nEcology\n\nWardens were obviously designed and programmed to guard objects, people, or locations. Although they have no life cycle to speak of, these robots do seem to possess certain behavioral characteristics that make them fascinating to Numerian scholars.\n\nThe warden's reactive armor is a matter of particular interest to the Technic League. Although the robots are still vulnerable to critical hits, their armor reduces the risk posed by this weakness. A few of the League's most talented members have devoted themselves to determining how the reactive armor works and how to replicate it. The secret appears to be in the material that comprises the robot's exoskeleton-which behaves like metal in all respects until struck by a powerful force, when it responds with a violent, fiery explosion. Amazingly, the explosive material restores itself over time, as long as the robot continues to function.\n\nHabitat & Society\n\nWardens, like many robots found in Numeria, follow strict internal programming that guides their actions. Their special programming, however, is somewhat more flexible than that of other robots. Wardens learn and adapt, especially when it comes to facing specialized types of foes.\n\nAs constructs built by ancient masters whose goals and intentions are almost unknowable, wardens have no\n\nsociety in the traditional sense of the word. They exist only to follow their programming to the best of their ability. Still, their ability to adapt and work together in small groups makes them formidable opponents for those who would seek treasures in the ancient caches scattered throughout Numeria.\n\nAlthough capable of speech, wardens communicate with each other by some other means. They coordinate efforts silently, and skillfully arrange patrols to maximize coverage of their assigned areas. As long as a warden is guarding something (whether by itself or as part of a group of wardens), it nearly always follows the orders of the creature that owns the object or location. Wardens demonstrate a clear understanding of their duties, and can apply their alien intelligence toward problem solving when the situation requires it. This makes them effective jailers as well, since they can use their incapacitating sound field against prisoners who attempt to escape-as well as on those who might try to break the prisoners out.\n\nWardensof Note Wardens appear to have been an apex design, for the same model has been found guarding many of the chambers in Silver Mount, as well as other scattered remnants of the massive vessel that fell from the sky so long ago. However, a few have been known to display different characteristics. Some of these alterations are intentional modifications made by people with great knowledge and skill. Other models may have even stranger origins.\n\nRed Terror (N warden robot ranger 7): The robot known as Red Terror guards a section of tunnels within the Red Redoubt of Karamoss. Red Terror appears to have been crafted using an alloy of djezet and steel (known as djezeteel). It's unclear whether the mad wizard Karamoss created the specialized warden robot using deciphered schematics or merely modified an existing construct. Either way, Red Terror is a skilled and ruthless hunter that relentlessly pursues intruders in its domain. Those adventurers who have encountered Red Terror claim that the robot actually seems to take pleasure in the gruesome deaths of its prey. The robot also seems to have some way to empower spellcasters it allies with and enhance the power of their spells.\n\nSilent Sentinel (CR 9): Explorers investigating ruins in the Felldales of western Numeria have reported encountering a unique version of the warden robot that can generate fields that cancel sound rather than induce nausea, earning it the name \"Silent Sentinel.\" This aura has the effect of a silence spell with a 30-foot radius centered on the warden, but the effect can't be dispelled or countered by magic. Instead of sonic disruptors, Silent Sentinel is equipped with integrated lasers that deal 2d8 points of fire damage. Based on recent reports from near the First Blade's Path, this specialized warden doesn't keep to just the Felldales.","ecology":"Wardens were obviously designed and programmed to guard objects, people, or locations. Although they have no life cycle to speak of, these robots do seem to possess certain behavioral characteristics that make them fascinating to Numerian scholars.\n\nThe warden's reactive armor is a matter of particular interest to the Technic League. Although the robots are still vulnerable to critical hits, their armor reduces the risk posed by this weakness. A few of the League's most talented members have devoted themselves to determining how the reactive armor works and how to replicate it. The secret appears to be in the material that comprises the robot's exoskeleton-which behaves like metal in all respects until struck by a powerful force, when it responds with a violent, fiery explosion. Amazingly, the explosive material restores itself over time, as long as the robot continues to function.","habitat_society":"Wardens, like many robots found in Numeria, follow strict internal programming that guides their actions. Their special programming, however, is somewhat more flexible than that of other robots. Wardens learn and adapt, especially when it comes to facing specialized types of foes.\n\nAs constructs built by ancient masters whose goals and intentions are almost unknowable, wardens have no\n\nsociety in the traditional sense of the word. They exist only to follow their programming to the best of their ability. Still, their ability to adapt and work together in small groups makes them formidable opponents for those who would seek treasures in the ancient caches scattered throughout Numeria.\n\nAlthough capable of speech, wardens communicate with each other by some other means. They coordinate efforts silently, and skillfully arrange patrols to maximize coverage of their assigned areas. As long as a warden is guarding something (whether by itself or as part of a group of wardens), it nearly always follows the orders of the creature that owns the object or location. Wardens demonstrate a clear understanding of their duties, and can apply their alien intelligence toward problem solving when the situation requires it. This makes them effective jailers as well, since they can use their incapacitating sound field against prisoners who attempt to escape-as well as on those who might try to break the prisoners out.\n\nWardensof Note Wardens appear to have been an apex design, for the same model has been found guarding many of the chambers in Silver Mount, as well as other scattered remnants of the massive vessel that fell from the sky so long ago. However, a few have been known to display different characteristics. Some of these alterations are intentional modifications made by people with great knowledge and skill. Other models may have even stranger origins.\n\nRed Terror (N warden robot ranger 7): The robot known as Red Terror guards a section of tunnels within the Red Redoubt of Karamoss. Red Terror appears to have been crafted using an alloy of djezet and steel (known as djezeteel). It's unclear whether the mad wizard Karamoss created the specialized warden robot using deciphered schematics or merely modified an existing construct. Either way, Red Terror is a skilled and ruthless hunter that relentlessly pursues intruders in its domain. Those adventurers who have encountered Red Terror claim that the robot actually seems to take pleasure in the gruesome deaths of its prey. The robot also seems to have some way to empower spellcasters it allies with and enhance the power of their spells.\n\nSilent Sentinel (CR 9): Explorers investigating ruins in the Felldales of western Numeria have reported encountering a unique version of the warden robot that can generate fields that cancel sound rather than induce nausea, earning it the name \"Silent Sentinel.\" This aura has the effect of a silence spell with a 30-foot radius centered on the warden, but the effect can't be dispelled or countered by magic. Instead of sonic disruptors, Silent Sentinel is equipped with integrated lasers that deal 2d8 points of fire damage. Based on recent reports from near the First Blade's Path, this specialized warden doesn't keep to just the Felldales."},{"name":"Wight Lord","cr":9,"xp":6400,"alignment":"LE","size":"Medium","type":"undead","init":5,"senses":[{"type":"darkvision","modifier":"60 ft."},{"type":"deathwatch"}],"ac":24,"ac_touch":11,"ac_flat_footed":23,"ac_mods":"+9 armor, +1 Dex, +4 natural","hp":115,"hd":"11d8+66","hdvalue":11,"fort":9,"ref":6,"will":9,"defensive_abilities":["channel resistance +4"],"dr":"10/cold iron or good","immunities":["undead traits"],"weaknesses":["resurrection vulnerability"],"speed":[{"type":"land","speed":30,"special":"40 ft. without armor"}],"melee":"+1 falchion +17 (2d4+11/15-20 plus energy drain) or slam +15 (1d6+1 plus energy drain)","space":"5 ft.","reach":"5 ft.","special_attacks":[{"type":"create spawn"},{"type":"energy drain","details":"1 level, DC 21"}],"spell_like_abilities_caster_level":9,"spell_like_abilities_concentration":9,"spell_like_abilities":[{"frequency":"at-will","spells":[{"spell":"deathwatch"}]},{"frequency":"1/day","spells":[{"spell":"haste"}]},{"frequency":"3/day","spells":[{"spell":"air walk"},{"spell":"greater command"}]}],"strength":24,"dexterity":13,"intelligence":13,"wisdom":15,"charisma":22,"baseatk":8,"cmb":15,"cmd":26,"feats":[{"feat":"Improved Initiative"},{"feat":"Lightning Reflexes"},{"feat":"Power Attack"},{"feat":"Quick Draw"},{"feat":"Vital Strike"},{"feat":"Weapon Focus (falchion)"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Climb","value":15},{"skill":"Intimidate","value":20},{"skill":"Perception","value":16},{"skill":"Sense Motive","value":16},{"skill":"Stealth","value":9}],"languages":["Common"],"environments":["any"],"organizations":["solitary","platoon (1 wight lord plus 4-6 advanced wights)"],"treasure":"none","description_visual":"This nearly skeletal figure wears the ancient armor of a long-dead king, and carries itself with a sort of regal pride.","source":"Undead Revisited","special_abilities":[{"type":"Create Spawn","kind":"Su","details":"Any humanoid creature that is slain by a wight lord becomes a wight itself in only 1d4 rounds. Although spawn so created are less powerful than wight lords, they are more powerful than typical wights, and are treated as wights with the advanced simple template. Spawn are under the command of the wight lord that created them and remain enslaved until its death, at which point they become fullfledged, free-willed advanced wights. They don't possess any of the abilities they had in life."},{"type":"Energy Drain","kind":"Su","details":"A wight lord inflicts a negative level each time it hits a foe with a slam attack. Like cairn wights, a wight lord can channel this negative energy through any weapon it wields, inflicting a negative level with each successful hit with the weapon."},{"type":"Resurrection Vulnerability","kind":"Su","details":"While a wight lord is vulnerable to resurrection magic, it isn't quite as vulnerable as a typical wight. A raise dead or similar spell cast on a wight lord staggers it for 1d6+1 rounds if it fails a Will save, but doesn't destroy the wight. Using the spell in this way doesn't require a material component."}],"description":"Dark princes and warlords of old, wight lords are undead monarchs. Where typical wights rise from a wide variety of individuals, wight lords rise from the bodies of despotic rulers or ruthless generals. Wight lords haunt the same ancient burial grounds and battlefields their lesser kin dwell in, but wight lords aren't satisfied by simply guarding their haunts against the living. They continue their reign as tyrants in death, ruling over undead armies and often compelling their unliving minions to wage war upon nearby towns or cities, sometimes even at the behest of bold and powerful necromancers. The statistics that are presented above represent the minimum power level of a wight lord. A wight lord can rise from the remains of any cruel or sadistic leader, but those who were higher than 11th level when they perished retain some of their previous life's knowledge-although not all of it. When this occurs, subtract 11 from the creature's previous number of class levels to determine the total number of class levels the wight lord possesses. Assign these class levels to the wight lord in a logical way-if it was a single-classed NPC in life, simply add more levels of that class to the wight lord. Multiclassed characters and those who possessed levels in prestige classes require more creativity in applying the class levels. The goal for building such a wight lord should be to approximate the themes and general abilities the creature had in life.","ecology":"","habitat_society":"","gear":"full plate, +1 falchion"},{"name":"Witchfire","cr":9,"xp":6400,"alignment":"CE","size":"Medium","type":"undead","subtypes":["incorporeal"],"init":10,"senses":[{"type":"darkvision","modifier":"60 ft."}],"ac":24,"ac_touch":24,"ac_flat_footed":17,"ac_mods":"+7 deflection, +6 Dex, +1 dodge","hp":115,"hd":"10d8+70","hdvalue":10,"fort":10,"ref":11,"will":10,"defensive_abilities":["incorporeal","witchflame"],"immunities":["fire","undead traits"],"speed":[{"type":"fly","speed":50,"maneuverability":"perfect"}],"melee":"incorporeal touch +13 (8d6 fire plus witchflame)","ranged":"witchflame bolt +13 (8d6 fire plus witchflame)","space":"5 ft.","reach":"5 ft.","spell_like_abilities_caster_level":9,"spell_like_abilities_concentration":9,"spell_like_abilities":[{"frequency":"at-will","spells":[{"spell":"dancing lights"},{"spell":"disguise self"},{"spell":"ghost sound"},{"spell":"invisibility"},{"spell":"pyrotechnics"},{"spell":"ray of enfeeblement"}]},{"frequency":"1/day","spells":[{"spell":"summon","details":"level 4, 2 will-o'- wisps 50%"}]}],"dexterity":22,"intelligence":17,"wisdom":16,"charisma":25,"baseatk":7,"cmb":13,"cmd":31,"feats":[{"feat":"Combat Reflexes"},{"feat":"Dodge"},{"feat":"Improved Initiative"},{"feat":"Lightning Reflexes"},{"feat":"Mobility"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Bluff","value":17},{"skill":"Fly","value":14},{"skill":"Intimidate","value":20},{"skill":"Knowledge (any two)","value":13},{"skill":"Perception","value":16},{"skill":"Sense Motive","value":16},{"skill":"Stealth","value":19}],"languages":["Auran","Common","Giant"],"sq":[{"type":"sound mimicry","details":"animal noises"}],"environments":["any swamps","any forests"],"organizations":["solitary","coven (3 witchfires and hags)"],"treasure":"standard","description_visual":"Bathed in sickly green flames, this insubstantial specter of a beautiful young woman floats just off the ground.","source":"PFRPG Bestiary 2","special_abilities":[{"type":"Witchflame","kind":"Su","details":"Any creature damaged by the incorporeal touch or ranged bolt attacks of a witchfire must succeed on a DC 22 Will save or become engulfed in sickly green flames. While these eerie flames deal no additional damage, the affected creature glows as per faerie fire and becomes sickened. While under the effects of the witchflame, the victim gains vulnerability to fire and takes half again as much damage (+50%) from fire attacks of any sort. This effect persists for 10 minutes. The supernatural flames can only be extinguished before this duration expires by a break enchantment, miracle, remove curse, or wish spell-the effective caster level of the witchflame is equal to the witchfire's HD (CL 10th for most witchfires). Any creature entering the same square as a witchfire or striking it with a melee attack must succeed on a DC 22 Will save or begin burning with witchflame, even if the attack would not otherwise harm the witchfire because of its incorporeal nature. A bolt of witchflame has a range of 60 ft. with no range increment. The save DCs are Charisma-based."}],"description":"When an exceptionally vile hag or witch dies with some malicious plot left incomplete, or proves too horridly tenacious to succumb to the call of death, the foul energies of these wicked old crones sometimes spawn incorporeal undead known as witchfires. These ghostly creatures appear much as they did in life, although the grotesque undead energy that births them makes them appear young and attractive and wreathes their insubstantial bodies in a powerful aura of sickly green flame, a ghostly fire referred to as \"witchflame\" in local legends.\n\nStrings of will-o'-wisps are often found in the immediate vicinity of witchfires and are typically led by the undead, leading scholars to speculate that the creatures feed off of a witchfire's flames and fury. Witchfires occasionally join or subjugate existing hag covens. A hag coven that includes a witchfire gains the following additional coven spell-like abilities: 3/day-blight, create undead, fire storm (DC 21), nightmare (DC 18), waves of exhaustion (DC 20). All abilities function at CL 9th, and save DCs are based on a Charisma score of 16. The use of these abilities functions identically to other coven abilities. Such covens must have at least one living hag, as covens of three witchfires gain no coven-related abilities.","ecology":"","habitat_society":""},{"name":"Yangethe","cr":9,"xp":6400,"alignment":"CE","size":"Large","type":"aberration","init":4,"senses":[{"type":"darkvision","modifier":"120 ft."}],"ac":23,"ac_touch":13,"ac_flat_footed":19,"ac_mods":"+4 Dex, +10 natural, -1 size","hp":115,"hd":"11d8+66","hdvalue":11,"fort":9,"ref":9,"will":12,"dr":"10/slashing or piercing","immunities":["cold","fear","mind-affecting effects"],"sr":20,"speed":[{"type":"land","speed":40}],"melee":"2 claws +14 (1d6+7), 4 tentacles +13 (1d6+3 plus grab)","space":"10 ft.","reach":"10 ft.","special_attacks":[{"type":"feeding tentacles"}],"spell_like_abilities_caster_level":10,"spell_like_abilities_concentration":20,"spell_like_abilities":[{"frequency":"constant","spells":[{"spell":"air walk"}]},{"frequency":"at-will","spells":[{"spell":"darkness"},{"spell":"telekinesis"},{"spell":"tree shape"}]},{"frequency":"1/day","spells":[{"spell":"demand"},{"spell":"psychic blast"}]},{"frequency":"3/day","spells":[{"spell":"fear"},{"spell":"quickened true strike"}]},{"frequency":"1/year","spells":[{"spell":"interplanetary teleport","details":"self plus 50 lbs. of objects only"}]}],"strength":24,"dexterity":18,"constitution":22,"intelligence":17,"wisdom":21,"charisma":17,"baseatk":8,"cmb":16,"cmb_special":"+4 vs. grapple","cmd":30,"cmd_special":"can't be tripped","feats":[{"feat":"Combat Casting"},{"feat":"Combat Expertise"},{"feat":"Lightning Reflexes"},{"feat":"Multiattack"},{"feat":"Quicken Spell-Like Ability (true strike)"},{"feat":"Weapon Focus (tentacles)"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Knowledge (arcana)","value":14},{"skill":"Knowledge (geography)","value":14},{"skill":"Knowledge (engineering)","value":17},{"skill":"Perception","value":19},{"skill":"Sense Motive","value":16},{"skill":"Spellcraft","value":17},{"skill":"Use Magic Device","value":14}],"languages":["Aklo","telepathy 60 ft."],"sq":[{"type":"no breath"}],"environments":["cold forests","any outer space"],"organizations":["solitary","pair","cluster (3-8)"],"treasure":"standard","description_visual":"This six-eyed horror looks something like a dead tree with claws, tentacles, spidery legs, and a mouth bulging with tentacles.","source":"The Dragon's Demand","special_abilities":[{"type":"Feeding Tentacles","kind":"Su","details":"As a standard action as part of maintaining a grapple, a yangethe can use its mouth tentacles to feed on a helpless or grappled creature by making a +14 melee touch attack. If it hits, the feeding tentacles siphon away the victim's emotions and deal 1d4 points of Charisma drain. The yangethe heals 5 points of damage for every point of Charisma it drains in this manner. As long as a creature continues to suffer this Charisma drain, each time it attempts to sleep it is affected by a nightmare spell (CL 10th, DC 20), experiencing terrifying dreams in which it relives the feeling of being fed upon over and over. All effects from the feeding tentacles are mind-affecting effects."},{"type":"Psychic Blast","kind":"Sp","details":"This spell-like ability functions as confusion, and also deals 10d6 points of nonlethal damage when it first affects foes (Will DC 21 half). This ability is the equivalent of a 5th-level spell."}],"description":"Bred by the Dominion of the Black, yangethes have, over the eons, developed keen intellects. On some planets, they've formed small, independent colonies that keep \"farms\" of victims on whose emotions they feed. The yangethes' ability to teleport across galaxies makes them remarkable as scouts or as the vanguards for an invasion. Unless slain violently, yangethes are immortal. They don't need to eat or drink to survive-though they will indulge in feeding for pleasure.","ecology":"","habitat_society":""},{"name":"Yithian","cr":9,"xp":6400,"alignment":"LN","size":"Large","type":"aberration","init":1,"senses":[{"type":"all-around vision"},{"type":"blindsense","modifier":"60 ft."},{"type":"darkvision","modifier":"60 ft."}],"ac":23,"ac_touch":10,"ac_flat_footed":22,"ac_mods":"+1 Dex, +13 natural, -1 size","hp":105,"hd":"14d8+42","hdvalue":14,"hp_mods":["fast healing 5"],"fort":9,"ref":5,"will":15,"dr":"10/magic","resists":[{"type":"acid","value":10},{"type":"cold","value":10},{"type":"fire","value":10}],"speed":[{"type":"land","speed":20},{"type":"climb","speed":10}],"melee":"2 pincers +15 (2d8+9/x3)","space":"10 ft.","reach":"10 ft.","special_attacks":[{"type":"amnesia"},{"type":"deadly pincers"},{"type":"mind swap"}],"spell_like_abilities_caster_level":15,"spell_like_abilities_concentration":18,"spell_like_abilities":[{"frequency":"at-will","spells":[{"spell":"astral projection","details":"self only"},{"spell":"detect thoughts"},{"spell":"hold monster"},{"spell":"modify memory"}]}],"strength":22,"dexterity":13,"constitution":17,"intelligence":24,"wisdom":19,"charisma":18,"baseatk":10,"cmb":17,"cmd":28,"feats":[{"feat":"Alertness"},{"feat":"Combat Expertise"},{"feat":"Great Fortitude"},{"feat":"Improved Great Fortitude"},{"feat":"Improved Iron Will"},{"feat":"Iron Will"},{"feat":"Vital Strike"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Climb","value":14},{"skill":"Diplomacy","value":18},{"skill":"Heal","value":18},{"skill":"Knowledge (arcana, engineering, geography, history)","value":21},{"skill":"Knowledge (planes)","value":24},{"skill":"Linguistics","value":21},{"skill":"Perception","value":25},{"skill":"Sense Motive","value":22},{"skill":"Use Magic Device","value":18}],"languages":["Aklo","Common","Yithian","20 other languages","telepathy 100 ft."],"sq":[{"type":"scholar"}],"environments":["any"],"organizations":["solitary","pair","band (3-9)","enclave (10-100)"],"treasure":"standard","description_visual":"This bizarre creature has a conical body topped with four tentacles tipped with pincers, tubes, and a tentacled, spherical head.","source":"PFRPG Bestiary 3","special_abilities":[{"type":"Amnesia","kind":"Su","details":"Once per day as a standard action, a yithian can attempt to inflict amnesia on a target it is able to communicate telepathically with. A target can resist this attack with a DC 21 Will save. If the target fails its save, it takes a permanent -4 penalty on Will saving throws and all skill checks, and loses all memories save for those the yithian chooses to leave intact. This effect can be cured by heal or greater restoration. This is a mind-affecting insanity effect. The save DC is Charisma-based."},{"type":"Deadly Pincers","kind":"Ex","details":"A yithian always applies 1-1/2 times its Strength modifier to damage dealt by its pincer attacks, and deals triple damage on a critical hit. Pincers are primary attacks for yithians."},{"type":"Mind Swap","kind":"Su","details":"As a full-round action, a yithian can trade minds with another living creature it is able to communicate telepathically with. This functions as magic jar, except the two minds trade bodies. An unwilling target can resist the mind swap with a DC 21 Will save, after which that particular yithian cannot attempt to swap minds with that creature again for 24 hours. The yithian can end the effect of this mind swap at any time and over any distance as a full-round action, instantly returning both minds to the proper bodies-if the yithian wishes, it may attempt to use its amnesia power on the other mind as a free action when it ends the mind swap in this way. This is a mind-affecting effect. The save DC is Charisma-based."},{"type":"Scholar","kind":"Ex","details":"Yithians treat all knowledge skills as class skills."}],"description":"Untold eons ago, the yithians inhabited a dying world. To escape their doomed planet, they cast their minds through time and space, eventually coming to rest in the strange, alien bodies they possess today. While these strange beings now reside in a distant galaxy, the yithians make use of their ability to astrally project to explore other planets, eager to find new worlds to explore.\n\nWhen a yithian arrives upon a new world, it often swaps minds with the creatures it encounters there so as to experience that world as if it were a native. Those who spend time in a yithian's body rarely tell of the strange times they have experienced, for yithians guard themselves well, and leave those they use in this manner amnesiacs who remember the truth only as fragmentary nightmares.","ecology":"","habitat_society":""},{"name":"Young Adult White Dragon","cr":9,"xp":6400,"alignment":"CE","size":"Large","type":"dragon","subtypes":["cold"],"init":5,"senses":[{"type":"dragon senses"},{"type":"snow vision"}],"ac":24,"ac_touch":10,"ac_flat_footed":23,"ac_mods":"+1 Dex, +14 natural, -1 size","hp":115,"hd":"11d12+44","hdvalue":11,"fort":11,"ref":8,"will":8,"dr":"5/magic","immunities":["cold","paralysis","sleep"],"sr":20,"weaknesses":["Vulnerability to fire"],"speed":[{"type":"land","speed":30},{"type":"burrow","speed":30},{"type":"fly","speed":200,"maneuverability":"poor"},{"type":"swim","speed":60}],"melee":"bite +17 (2d6+9/19-20), 2 claws +16 (1d8+6), 2 wings +11 (1d6+3), tail slap +11 (1d8+9)","space":"10 ft.","reach":"5 ft. (10 ft. with bite)","special_attacks":[{"type":"breath weapon","details":"40-ft. cone, DC 19, 10d4 cold"}],"spell_like_abilities_caster_level":11,"spell_like_abilities_concentration":15,"spell_like_abilities":[{"frequency":"at-will","spells":[{"spell":"fog cloud"},{"spell":"gust of wind"}]}],"strength":23,"dexterity":12,"constitution":19,"intelligence":10,"wisdom":13,"charisma":10,"baseatk":11,"cmb":18,"cmd":29,"cmd_special":"+4 vs. trip","feats":[{"feat":"Alertness"},{"feat":"Flyby Attack"},{"feat":"Improved Critical (bite)"},{"feat":"Improved Initiative"},{"feat":"Power Attack"},{"feat":"Weapon Focus (bite)"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Fly","value":9},{"skill":"Intimidate","value":14},{"skill":"Perception","value":19},{"skill":"Spellcraft","value":14},{"skill":"Stealth","value":11},{"skill":"Swim","value":28}],"languages":["Draconic"],"sq":[{"type":"icewalking"},{"type":"ice shape"}],"environments":["cold mountains"],"organizations":["solitary"],"treasure":"triple","description_visual":"This dragon's scales are a frosty white. Its head is crowned with slender horns, with a thin membrane stretched between them.","group":"Chromatic Dragon","source":"PFRPG Bestiary","special_abilities":[{"type":"Ice Shape","kind":"Su","details":"A young white dragon can shape ice and snow at will. This ability functions as stone shape, but only targeting ice and snow, not stone. A white dragon's caster level for this effect is equal to its Hit Dice."},{"type":"Icewalking","kind":"Ex","details":"This ability works like the spider climb spell, but the surfaces the dragon climbs must be icy. The dragon can move across icy surfaces without penalty and doesn't need to make Acrobatics checks to run or charge on ice."},{"type":"Snow Vision","kind":"Ex","details":"A very young white dragon learns to see perfectly well in snowy conditions. A white dragon doesn't suffer any penalties to Perception checks while in snow."}],"description":"Although most consider it to be the weakest and most feral of the chromatic dragons, the white dragon makes up for its lack of cunning with sheer ferocity. White dragons dwell on remote, frozen mountaintops and in arctic lowlands, making their home in glittering caves full of ice and snow. They prefer their meals completely frozen.","ecology":"","habitat_society":""},{"name":"Young Blue Dragon","cr":9,"xp":6400,"alignment":"LE","size":"Large","type":"dragon","subtypes":["earth"],"init":5,"senses":[{"type":"dragon senses"}],"ac":21,"ac_touch":10,"ac_flat_footed":20,"ac_mods":"+1 Dex, +11 natural, -1 size","hp":95,"hd":"10d12+30","hdvalue":10,"fort":10,"ref":8,"will":8,"immunities":["electricity","paralysis","sleep"],"speed":[{"type":"land","speed":40},{"type":"burrow","speed":20},{"type":"fly","speed":200,"maneuverability":"poor"}],"melee":"bite +15 (2d6+7), 2 claws +14 (1d8+5), 2 wings +12 (1d6+2), tail slap +12 (1d8+7)","space":"10 ft.","reach":"5 ft. (10 ft. with bite)","special_attacks":[{"type":"breath weapon","details":"80-ft. line, DC 18, 6d8 electricity"},{"type":"desert thirst","details":"DC 16"}],"spell_like_abilities_caster_level":10,"spell_like_abilities_concentration":13,"spell_like_abilities":[{"frequency":"at-will","spells":[{"spell":"ghost sound"}]}],"strength":21,"dexterity":12,"constitution":17,"intelligence":12,"wisdom":13,"charisma":12,"baseatk":10,"cmb":16,"cmd":27,"cmd_special":"+4 vs. trip","feats":[{"feat":"Dazzling Display"},{"feat":"Improved Initiative"},{"feat":"Multiattack"},{"feat":"Shatter Defenses"},{"feat":"Weapon Focus (bite)"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Bluff","value":14},{"skill":"Fly","value":8},{"skill":"Intimidate","value":14},{"skill":"Knowledge (local)","value":14},{"skill":"Perception","value":14},{"skill":"Stealth","value":10},{"skill":"Survival","value":14}],"languages":["Common","Draconic"],"sq":[{"type":"sound imitation"}],"environments":["warm deserts"],"organizations":["solitary"],"treasure":"triple","description_visual":"With scales the color of the desert sky, this large, serpentine dragon moves with an unsettling grace.","group":"Chromatic Dragon","source":"PFRPG Bestiary","special_abilities":[{"type":"Desert Thirst","kind":"Su","details":"A blue dragon can cast create water at will (CL equals its HD). Alternatively, it can destroy an equal amount of liquid in a 10-foot burst. Unattended liquids are instantly reduced to sand. Liquid-based magic items (such as potions) and items in a creature's possession must succeed on a Will save (DC equal to the dragon's breath weapon) or be destroyed. The save DC is Charisma-based."},{"type":"Electricity Aura","kind":"Su","details":"An adult blue dragon is surrounded by an aura of electricity. Creatures within 5 ft. take 1d6 points of electricity damage at the beginning of the dragon's turn. An old dragon's aura extends to 10 ft. An ancient dragon's damage increases to 2d6."},{"type":"Mirage","kind":"Su","details":"An old or older blue dragon can make itself appear to be in two places at once as a free action for a number of rounds per day equal to its Hit Dice. This ability functions as project image but the dragon can use its breath weapon through the mirage."},{"type":"Sandstorm","kind":"Su","details":"As a standard action, a great wyrm blue dragon can create a sandstorm centered on itself with a radius of 1,200 ft. Creatures other than the dragon inside the storm take 2d6 points of damage per round in addition to the normal sandstorm penalties. This sandstorm lasts for up to 1 hour, but can be dismissed by the dragon as a free action."},{"type":"Sound Imitation","kind":"Ex","details":"A very young or older blue dragon can mimic any voice or sound it has heard by making a successful Bluff check against a listener's Sense Motive check."},{"type":"Spell-Like Abilities","kind":"Sp","details":"A blue dragon gains the following spell-like abilities, usable at will upon reaching the listed age category. Young-ghost sound; Juvenile-minor image; Adult-ventriloquism; Old-hallucinatory terrain; Ancient- veil; Great wyrm-mirage arcana."},{"type":"Storm Breath","kind":"Su","details":"An ancient or older blue dragon can use its breath weapon to create a storm of lightning. This functions as call lightning storm, but the damage is equal to the dragon's breath weapon. The dragon can call down 1 bolt per round as a free action for 1d6 rounds. The save DC is equal to the dragon's breath weapon DC. Additional uses of this ability extend the duration by an additional 1d6 rounds. Age Category S pecial Abilities Caster Level Wyrmling Desert thirst, immune to electricity - Very young Sound imitation - Young Ghost sound - Juvenile Frightful presence, minor image 1st Young adult DR 5/magic, spell resistance 3rd Adult Electricity aura, ventriloquism 5th Mature adult DR 10/magic 7th Old Mirage, hallucinatory terrain 9th Very old DR 15/magic 11th Ancient Storm breath, veil 13th Wyrm DR 20/magic 15th Great wyrm Sandstorm, mirage arcana 17th."}],"description":"Blue dragons are consummate schemers and obsessively orderly. In combat, blue dragons prefer to surprise foes if possible, and are not above retreating if the odds turn against them. They prefer to lair near those that they control, sometimes even within the confines of a city.","ecology":"","habitat_society":""},{"name":"Young Bronze Dragon","cr":9,"xp":6400,"alignment":"LG","size":"Large","type":"dragon","subtypes":["water"],"init":1,"senses":[{"type":"dragon senses"}],"ac":21,"ac_touch":10,"ac_flat_footed":20,"ac_mods":"+1 Dex, +11 natural, -1 size","hp":95,"hd":"10d12+30","hdvalue":10,"fort":10,"ref":8,"will":10,"immunities":["electricity","paralysis","sleep"],"speed":[{"type":"land","speed":40},{"type":"fly","speed":200,"maneuverability":"poor"},{"type":"swim","speed":60}],"melee":"bite +14 (2d6+7), 2 claws +14 (1d8+5), 2 wings +12 (1d6+2), tail +12 (1d8+7)","space":"5 ft.","reach":"5 ft.","special_attacks":[{"type":"breath weapon","details":"80-ft. line, DC 18, 6d6 electricity"},{"type":"repulsion breath"}],"spell_like_abilities_caster_level":10,"spell_like_abilities_concentration":13,"spell_like_abilities":[{"frequency":"at-will","spells":[{"spell":"speak with animals"}]}],"spellsknown_caster_level":1,"spellsknown_concentration":4,"spellsknown":[{"spell_level":1,"spell_slots":4,"spells":[{"spell":"alarm"},{"spell":"obscuring mist"}]},{"spell_level":0,"spell_slots":99,"spells":[{"spell":"detect magic"},{"spell":"light"},{"spell":"message"},{"spell":"resistance"}]}],"strength":21,"dexterity":12,"constitution":17,"intelligence":16,"wisdom":17,"charisma":16,"baseatk":10,"cmb":16,"cmd":27,"cmd_special":"+4 vs. trip","feats":[{"feat":"Alertness"},{"feat":"Flyby Attack"},{"feat":"Multiattack"},{"feat":"Power Attack"},{"feat":"Vital Strike"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Diplomacy","value":16},{"skill":"Fly","value":8},{"skill":"Intimidate","value":16},{"skill":"Knowledge (arcana)","value":16},{"skill":"Perception","value":20},{"skill":"Sense Motive","value":20},{"skill":"Spellcraft","value":16},{"skill":"Stealth","value":10},{"skill":"Swim","value":26}],"languages":["Aquan","Common","Draconic","Elven"],"sq":[{"type":"change shape"},{"type":"water breathing"}],"environments":["temperate coastlines"],"organizations":["solitary"],"treasure":"triple","description_visual":"This sleek dragon is covered in dull metallic scales that range in color from shining bronze to mottled blue.","group":"Metallic Dragon","source":"PFRPG Bestiary","special_abilities":[{"type":"Change Shape","kind":"Su","details":"A young or older bronze dragon can take any animal or humanoid form 3/day as if using polymorph."},{"type":"Electricity Aura","kind":"Su","details":"An old or older bronze dragon has an aura of electricity. All creatures within 5 ft. take 1d6 points of electricity damage at the start of the dragon's turn. An ancient dragon's aura is 10 ft. A great wyrm's damage increases to 2d6. A bronze dragon can suppress this aura at will."},{"type":"Repulsion Breath","kind":"Su","details":"Instead of a line of electricity, a bronze dragon can breathe a cone of repulsion gas. Targets must make a Will save or be compelled to do nothing but move away from the dragon for 1d6 rounds plus 1 round per age category. This is a mind-affecting compulsion effect."},{"type":"Spell-Like Abilities","kind":"Sp","details":"A bronze dragon gains the following spell-like abilities, usable at will upon reaching the listed age category. Very young-speak with animals; Juvenile-create food and water; Adult-fog cloud; Old-detect thoughts; Ancient-control water; Great wyrm-control weather."},{"type":"Tidal Wave","kind":"Su","details":"A great wyrm bronze dragon can cause the sea to rise up and crush his enemies once per day as a standard action. This affects an area of coastline 120 ft. in length and targets all creatures within 40 ft. of the shore-treat the targets as if struck by an avalanche. Treat all creatures as if they were in the bury zone. The save DC to halve this damage is equal to the dragon's breath weapon DC. Those who fail their saves take full damage and are drawn 60 ft. off shore and deposited 20 ft. under the surface on the round after the wave hits."},{"type":"Vortex","kind":"Ex","details":"Once per day, an ancient or older bronze dragon can create a vortex as a standard action, just like an elder water elemental. A bronze dragon can maintain this vortex for 1 round per age category."},{"type":"Water Breathing","kind":"Ex","details":"A bronze dragon breathes water and can use its breath weapon, spells, and abilities underwater."},{"type":"Wave Mastery","kind":"Su","details":"For up to 10 minutes per age category per day, a juvenile bronze dragon, along with creatures or vessels within 50 ft., can move at twice its normal speed in water. Age Category S pecial Abilities C aster Level Wyrmling Immunity to electricity, - repulsion breath, water breathing Very young Speak with animals - Young Change shape 1st Juvenile Wave mastery, create food and water 3rd Young adult DR 5/magic, spell resistance 5th Adult frightful presence, fog cloud 7th Mature adult DR 10/magic 9th Old Electricity aura, detect thoughts 11th Very old DR 15/magic 13th Ancient Vortex, control water 15th Wyrm DR 20/magic 17th Great wyrm Tidal wave, control weather 19th."}],"description":"Bronze dragons have been known to ally with travelers and adventurers if the cause and reward is right and just.","ecology":"","habitat_society":""},{"name":"Young Cloud Dragon","cr":9,"xp":6400,"alignment":"CN","size":"Large","type":"dragon","subtypes":["air","extraplanar"],"init":0,"senses":[{"type":"dragon senses"},{"type":"mist vision"}],"ac":20,"ac_touch":9,"ac_flat_footed":20,"ac_mods":"+11 natural, -1 size","hp":95,"hd":"10d12+30","hdvalue":10,"fort":10,"ref":7,"will":8,"immunities":["electricity","paralysis","sleep"],"speed":[{"type":"land","speed":40},{"type":"fly","speed":200,"maneuverability":"poor"},{"type":"swim","speed":40}],"melee":"bite +13 (2d6+6), 2 claws +14 (1d8+4), 2 wings +11 (1d6+2), tail slap +11 (1d8+6)","space":"5 ft.","reach":"5 ft.","special_attacks":[{"type":"breath weapon","details":"40-ft. cone, 6d8 electricity, DC 18"}],"spell_like_abilities_caster_level":10,"spell_like_abilities_concentration":13,"spell_like_abilities":[{"frequency":"at-will","spells":[{"spell":"fog cloud"},{"spell":"obscuring mist"}]}],"strength":18,"dexterity":11,"constitution":17,"intelligence":12,"wisdom":16,"charisma":15,"baseatk":10,"cmb":14,"cmd":26,"cmd_special":"+4 vs. trip","feats":[{"feat":"Dazzling Display"},{"feat":"Multiattack"},{"feat":"Power Attack"},{"feat":"Skill Focus (Diplomacy)"},{"feat":"Weapon Focus (claws)"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Appraise","value":14},{"skill":"Diplomacy","value":21},{"skill":"Fly","value":7},{"skill":"Intimidate","value":15},{"skill":"Knowledge (planes)","value":14},{"skill":"Perception","value":16},{"skill":"Stealth","value":9},{"skill":"Swim","value":12}],"languages":["Auran","Draconic"],"environments":["any air (Plane of Air)"],"organizations":["solitary"],"treasure":"triple","description_visual":"The blue-white scales of this four-horned dragon exude wisps of fog. The dragon's snout is short but filled with sharp teeth.","group":"Primal Dragon","source":"PFRPG Bestiary 2","special_abilities":[{"type":"Cloud Form","kind":"Su","details":"An adult or older cloud dragon can change itself into a cloudy vapor as a swift action for a number of rounds per day equal to its Hit Dice. This ability functions as gaseous form but the dragon's fly speed is unchanged."},{"type":"Cloud Breath","kind":"Su","details":"A great wyrm cloud dragon's breath weapon creates a cloud that persists in its cone shape for 1d4 rounds. Treat this cloud as a fog cloud that deals electricity damage equal to half the dragon's breath weapon damage to any creature that ends its turn still within the cloud (Reflex save halves the damage-DC equals the dragon's breath weapon save DC)."},{"type":"Mist Vision","kind":"Su","details":"A cloud dragon can see through fog, clouds, and similar obscuring effects with perfect clarity."},{"type":"Spell-Like Abilities","kind":"Sp","details":"A cloud dragon gains the following spell-like abilities, usable at will (unless indicated otherwise) on reaching the listed age category. Very young-obscuring mist; Young-fog cloud; Adult-solid fog; Old-cloudkill (3/day); Ancient-wind walk; Great wyrm-storm of vengeance (1/day)."},{"type":"Thundering Bite","kind":"Su","details":"An ancient or older cloud dragon's bite makes a thundering crash whenever it attacks, dealing an additional 2d6 points of sonic damage. A great wyrm's thundering bite deals an additional 4d6 sonic damage."}],"description":"Cloud dragons stay out of the complicated political schemes and obsessions of other dragons (especially the chromatic dragons), preferring to live their lives freely and as the whim to travel strikes them. Exploration and viewing new lands from far above are the cloud dragon's greatest joy, rivaled only by speaking with new creatures and gaining exotic treasures from them. They keep lairs on high mountain peaks, but are often away on journeys of discovery, returning home only when they've claimed a new treasure that needs to be placed in safekeeping back home.","ecology":"","habitat_society":""},{"name":"Young Lunar Dragon","cr":9,"xp":6400,"alignment":"CN","size":"Large","type":"dragon","init":0,"senses":[{"type":"dragon senses"},{"type":"see in darkness"}],"ac":21,"ac_touch":9,"ac_flat_footed":21,"ac_mods":"+12 natural, -1 size","hp":105,"hd":"10d12+40","hdvalue":10,"fort":10,"ref":7,"will":11,"defensive_abilities":["reflected light"],"immunities":["cold","paralysis","sleep"],"speed":[{"type":"land","speed":40},{"type":"burrow","speed":20},{"type":"fly","speed":200,"maneuverability":"poor"}],"melee":"bite +14 (2d6+7), 2 claws +14 (1d8+5), 2 wings +12 (1d6+2), tail slap +12 (1d8+7)","space":"10 ft.","reach":"5 ft. (10 ft. with bite)","special_attacks":[{"type":"bewildering breath"},{"type":"breath weapon","details":"80-ft. line, 6d8 cold, DC 18"},{"type":"moonsilver"}],"spell_like_abilities_caster_level":10,"spell_like_abilities_concentration":13,"spell_like_abilities":[{"frequency":"at-will","spells":[{"spell":"dancing lights"}]}],"spellsknown_caster":"sorcerer","spellsknown_caster_level":1,"spellsknown_concentration":4,"spellsknown":[{"spell_level":1,"spell_slots":4,"spells":[{"spell":"comprehend languages"},{"spell":"mage armor"}]},{"spell_level":0,"spell_slots":99,"spells":[{"spell":"detect magic"},{"spell":"light"},{"spell":"mage hand"},{"spell":"read magic"}]}],"strength":21,"dexterity":11,"constitution":16,"intelligence":16,"wisdom":18,"charisma":17,"baseatk":10,"cmb":16,"cmd":26,"cmd_special":"+4 vs. trip","feats":[{"feat":"Flyby Attack"},{"feat":"Multiattack"},{"feat":"Power Attack"},{"feat":"Step Up"},{"feat":"Toughness"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Diplomacy","value":16},{"skill":"Fly","value":7},{"skill":"Intimidate","value":16},{"skill":"Knowledge (arcana, geography, history, local, nature)","value":10},{"skill":"Perception","value":17},{"skill":"Sense Motive","value":17},{"skill":"Spellcraft","value":16},{"skill":"Use Magic Device","value":16}],"languages":["Aklo","Auran","Common","Draconic"],"sq":[{"type":"no breath"},{"type":"starflight"}],"environments":["any vacuum"],"organizations":["solitary"],"treasure":"triple","description_visual":"A shimmering halo surrounds this regal dragon's spine-crowned head, and its vast wings ripple like milky gossamer lit by the moon.","group":"Outer Dragon","source":"PFRPG Bestiary 4","special_abilities":[{"type":"Absolute Cold","kind":"Su","details":"An old or older lunar dragon's breath weapon can affect creatures immune to cold damage. A creature immune to cold damage still takes half damage from the breath weapon (no damage with a successful saving throw). Resistant creatures' cold resistance is treated as 10 less than normal."},{"type":"Alien Presence","kind":"Su","details":"A lunar dragon's alien presence affects opponents that fail their saves as touch of idiocy (or as feeblemind for creatures with 4 or fewer Hit Dice) for 5d6 rounds. This is a mind-affecting compulsion effect."},{"type":"Bewildering Breath","kind":"Su","details":"A creature that fails its saving throw against a lunar dragon's breath weapon emits light (as faerie fire) and is dazzled for 1d4 rounds. If the lunar dragon is adult or older, the creature is also confused for 1d4 rounds."},{"type":"Moonsilver","kind":"Ex","details":"A lunar dragon's natural weapons are treated as silver for the purpose of overcoming damage reduction."},{"type":"Reflect Rays","kind":"Su","details":"Rays and ranged touch effects that strike an ancient or older lunar dragon but fail to overcome its spell resistance are reflected back at their source, using the original attack roll to determine whether they hit."},{"type":"Reflected Light","kind":"Ex","details":"A very young or older lunar dragon can't be blinded or dazzled by bright light or patterns."}],"description":"Lunar dragons frequently interact with mortals, spending long hours watching the activities occurring on planets that interest them.","ecology":"","habitat_society":""},{"name":"Young Sky Dragon","cr":9,"xp":6400,"alignment":"LG","size":"Large","type":"dragon","subtypes":["air"],"init":1,"senses":[{"type":"cloud sight"},{"type":"dragon senses"}],"ac":22,"ac_touch":10,"ac_flat_footed":21,"ac_mods":"+1 Dex, +12 natural, -1 size","hp":95,"hd":"10d12+30","hdvalue":10,"fort":10,"ref":10,"will":10,"immunities":["electricity","paralysis","sleep"],"speed":[{"type":"land","speed":40},{"type":"fly","speed":200,"maneuverability":"good"}],"melee":"bite +14 (2d6+7), 2 claws +14 (1d8+5), gore +14 (1d8+7), tail slap +12 (1d8+7)","space":"10 ft.","reach":"5 ft. (10 ft. with bite and gore)","special_attacks":[{"type":"breath weapon","details":"40-ft. cone, 6d8 electricity damage, DC 18"}],"spell_like_abilities_caster_level":10,"spell_like_abilities_concentration":13,"spell_like_abilities":[{"frequency":"at-will","spells":[{"spell":"detect evil"}]}],"spellsknown_caster_level":1,"spellsknown_concentration":4,"spellsknown":[{"spell_level":1,"spell_slots":4,"spells":[{"spell":"obscuring mist"},{"spell":"shocking grasp"}]},{"spell_level":0,"spell_slots":99,"spells":[{"spell":"disrupt undead"},{"spell":"mending"},{"spell":"message"},{"spell":"read magic"}]}],"strength":21,"dexterity":12,"constitution":17,"intelligence":16,"wisdom":17,"charisma":16,"baseatk":10,"cmb":16,"cmd":27,"cmd_special":"+4 vs. trip","feats":[{"feat":"Flyby Attack"},{"feat":"Hover"},{"feat":"Lightning Reflexes"},{"feat":"Multiattack"},{"feat":"Skill Focus (Perception)"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Diplomacy","value":16},{"skill":"Fly","value":16},{"skill":"Heal","value":16},{"skill":"Knowledge (arcana, religion)","value":16},{"skill":"Perception","value":22},{"skill":"Perform (sing)","value":13},{"skill":"Sense Motive","value":16},{"skill":"Spellcraft","value":16}],"languages":["Auran","Common","Draconic"],"sq":[{"type":"borne aloft"},{"type":"change shape"}],"environments":["temperate mountains","warm mountains"],"organizations":["solitary"],"treasure":"triple","description_visual":"Although wingless, this dragon twists gracefully though the sky, its scales ref lecting the shifting hues of the heavens.","group":"Imperial Dragon","source":"PFRPG Bestiary 3","special_abilities":[{"type":"Borne Aloft","kind":"Su","details":"Old or younger sky dragons fly with good maneuverability while all older sky dragons have perfect."},{"type":"Celestial Emissary","kind":"Su","details":"Three times per day, a great wyrm sky dragon can imbue others with the celestial aspect of the oracle spell divine vessel, but it can only be cast on another willing creature of good alignment."},{"type":"Change Shape","kind":"Su","details":"A young or older sky dragon can assume any humanoid form three times per day as if using polymorph."},{"type":"Cloud Sight","kind":"Su","details":"A very young or older sky dragon's sight isn't impeded by clouds or fog, or by spells that create areas of fog."},{"type":"Grounding Breath","kind":"Su","details":"Any flying creature damaged by the breath weapon of an ancient or older sky dragon must make a Fortitude save with the same DC as the sky dragon's breath weapon or lose the ability to fly for 1d4 rounds."},{"type":"Primal Lightning","kind":"Su","details":"An old or older sky dragon's breath weapon can affect creatures normally immune or resistant to electricity damage. A creature immune to electricity damage still takes half damage from the breath weapon (no damage with a successful saving throw). Resistant creatures' electricity resistance is treated as 10 less than normal."}],"description":"Benevolent and noble, sky dragons, or tienlungs, are fearsome champions of good and protectors of those in need. They are often sought out for their wise council, which they grant only to the deserving and true.","ecology":"","habitat_society":""},{"name":"Young Solar Dragon","cr":9,"xp":6400,"alignment":"LN","size":"Large","type":"dragon","subtypes":["fire"],"init":6,"senses":[{"type":"dragon senses"},{"type":"see in darkness"}],"ac":21,"ac_touch":11,"ac_flat_footed":19,"ac_mods":"+2 Dex, +10 natural, -1 size","hp":115,"hd":"11d12+44","hdvalue":11,"fort":10,"ref":11,"will":10,"immunities":["fire","paralysis","sleep"],"weaknesses":["vulnerable to cold"],"speed":[{"type":"land","speed":50},{"type":"fly","speed":200,"maneuverability":"poor"}],"melee":"bite +16 (1d8+9), 2 claws +16 (1d6+6), 2 wings +14 (1d6+3)","space":"10 ft.","reach":"5 ft. (10 ft. with bite)","special_attacks":[{"type":"breath weapon","details":"80-ft. line, 6d10 fire, DC 18"},{"type":"channel life","details":"6/day"},{"type":"primal fire"}],"spell_like_abilities_caster_level":1,"spell_like_abilities_concentration":4,"spell_like_abilities":[{"frequency":"at-will","spells":[{"spell":"detect magic"}]}],"spellsknown_caster":"sorcerer","spellsknown_caster_level":1,"spellsknown_concentration":4,"spellsknown":[{"spell_level":1,"spell_slots":4,"spells":[{"spell":"color spray"},{"spell":"mage armor"}]},{"spell_level":0,"spell_slots":99,"spells":[{"spell":"bleed"},{"spell":"detect poison"},{"spell":"flare"},{"spell":"read magic"}]}],"strength":22,"dexterity":15,"constitution":16,"intelligence":15,"wisdom":12,"charisma":17,"baseatk":11,"cmb":18,"cmd":30,"cmd_special":"+4 vs. trip","feats":[{"feat":"Improved Initiative"},{"feat":"Iron Will"},{"feat":"Lightning Reflexes"},{"feat":"Multiattack"},{"feat":"Quick Channel"},{"feat":"Toughness"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Diplomacy","value":17},{"skill":"Fly","value":10},{"skill":"Knowledge (arcana)","value":16},{"skill":"Knowledge (history)","value":16},{"skill":"Knowledge (nature)","value":16},{"skill":"Knowledge (planes)","value":16},{"skill":"Perception","value":15},{"skill":"Sense Motive","value":15}],"languages":["Celestial","Common","Draconic"],"sq":[{"type":"no breath"},{"type":"starflight"}],"environments":["any vacuum"],"organizations":["solitary"],"treasure":"triple","description_visual":"This regal dragon glows like the sun. Its burnished wings shimmer the color of flames, and a crown of horns decorates its head.","group":"Outer Dragon","source":"PFRPG Bestiary 4","special_abilities":[{"type":"Alien Presence","kind":"Su","details":"A creature that fails its saving throw against a solar dragon's alien presence is blinded for 5d6 rounds (or permanently if it has 4 Hit Dice or fewer)."},{"type":"Beam of Light","kind":"Su","details":"A great wyrm solar dragon can transform itself into a beam of pure light and travel to any location it can see as a move action. This travel must be in a straight line, but otherwise the dragon can travel anywhere that light can enter."},{"type":"Channel Life","kind":"Su","details":"A solar dragon can channel positive energy a number of times per day equal to 3 + its Charisma modifier, using its age category + 2 as its cleric level. This energy can be used only to heal living creatures."},{"type":"Channel Radiation","kind":"Su","details":"An old or older solar dragon can use its channel life ability to instead channel radiation that deals an equal amount of damage to living creatures. A living creature that succeeds at a Fortitude save takes half damage."},{"type":"Primal Fire","kind":"Su","details":"A very young or older solar dragon's breath weapon can affect creatures normally immune or resistant to fire damage. A creature immune to fire damage still takes half damage from the breath weapon (no damage with a successful saving throw). A resistant creature's fire resistance is treated as 10 less than normal."}],"description":"Arrogant and proud, solar dragons see themselves as the originators of light and life in the vastness of space. They treat all living creatures as their own creations.","ecology":"","habitat_society":""},{"name":"Young Void Dragon","cr":9,"xp":6400,"alignment":"NE","size":"Large","type":"dragon","init":2,"senses":[{"type":"dragon senses"},{"type":"see in darkness"}],"ac":22,"ac_touch":11,"ac_flat_footed":20,"ac_mods":"+2 Dex, +11 natural, -1 size","hp":95,"hd":"10d12+30","hdvalue":10,"fort":10,"ref":9,"will":10,"immunities":["cold","confusion","insanity effects","paralysis","sleep"],"speed":[{"type":"land","speed":40},{"type":"fly","speed":200,"maneuverability":"good"}],"melee":"bite +15 (2d6+7 plus obliterate), 2 claws +14 (1d8+5), 2 wings +12 (1d6+2), tail slap +12 (1d8+7)","space":"10 ft.","reach":"5 ft. (10 ft. with bite)","special_attacks":[{"type":"breath weapon","details":"40-ft. cone, 6d8 cold, DC 18"},{"type":"obliterate","details":"DC 18"},{"type":"suffocating breath","details":"DC 18"}],"spell_like_abilities_caster_level":10,"spell_like_abilities_concentration":13,"spell_like_abilities":[{"frequency":"at-will","spells":[{"spell":"ray of enfeeblement"}]}],"spellsknown_caster":"sorcerer","spellsknown_caster_level":1,"spellsknown_concentration":4,"spellsknown":[{"spell_level":1,"spell_slots":4,"spells":[{"spell":"hypnotism"},{"spell":"mage armor"}]},{"spell_level":0,"spell_slots":99,"spells":[{"spell":"detect magic"},{"spell":"mage hand"},{"spell":"message"},{"spell":"read magic"}]}],"strength":21,"dexterity":14,"constitution":17,"intelligence":16,"wisdom":13,"charisma":16,"baseatk":10,"cmb":16,"cmd":28,"cmd_special":"+4 vs. trip","feats":[{"feat":"Flyby Attack"},{"feat":"Iron Will"},{"feat":"Multiattack"},{"feat":"Weapon Focus (bite)"},{"feat":"Wingover"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Acrobatics","value":12},{"skill":"Bluff","value":16},{"skill":"Diplomacy","value":13},{"skill":"Fly","value":19},{"skill":"Intimidate","value":16},{"skill":"Knowledge (arcana)","value":13},{"skill":"Knowledge (planes)","value":13},{"skill":"Perception","value":14},{"skill":"Sense Motive","value":14},{"skill":"Spellcraft","value":11},{"skill":"Stealth","value":11},{"skill":"Survival","value":8}],"languages":["Abyssal","Aklo","Draconic","Infernal"],"sq":[{"type":"agile"},{"type":"no breath"},{"type":"starflight"}],"environments":["any vacuum"],"organizations":["solitary"],"treasure":"triple","description_visual":"This dragon's ebony scales and horns are flecked with a substance that glows an eerie green. The folds of its wings reflect a starry sky.","group":"Outer Dragon","source":"PFRPG Bestiary 4","special_abilities":[{"type":"Agile","kind":"Ex","details":"Void dragons have good aerial maneuverability regardless of their age or size."},{"type":"Alien Presence","kind":"Su","details":"A void dragon's alien presence causes an opponent that fails its save to be overcome with dizziness, becoming sickened (or nauseated if the target has 4 or fewer Hit Dice) for 5d6 rounds."},{"type":"Obliterate","kind":"Su","details":"A young or older void dragon's bite deals an additional 2d6 points of negative energy damage. A creature reduced to 0 or fewer hit points by this attack must succeed at a Fortitude save or be immediately slain and reduced to ashes (as the disintegrate spell). The save DC is Constitution-based."},{"type":"Suffocating Breath","kind":"Su","details":"Instead of dealing cold damage, a very young or older void dragon can breathe a cone-shaped suffocation effect. An air-dependent creature that fails its Fortitude save suffocates for a number of rounds equal to the dragon's age category. The save DC is Constitution-based."},{"type":"Void Gaze","kind":"Su","details":"A creature within 30 ft. of an adult or older void dragon must succeed at a Will save or become confused for 1d6 rounds. This gaze attack is a mind-affecting effect. The save DC is Charisma-based."}],"description":"Void dragons have been tainted by long exposure to the terrible alien entities that dwell in deep space. Though some continue to struggle against the inevitable tide of annihilation, many have embraced the encroaching void and exist only to feed and destroy.","ecology":"","habitat_society":""},{"name":"Yrthak","cr":9,"xp":6400,"alignment":"N","size":"Huge","type":"magical beast","init":6,"senses":[{"type":"blindsight","modifier":"120 ft."}],"ac":23,"ac_touch":11,"ac_flat_footed":20,"ac_mods":"+2 Dex, +1 dodge, +12 natural, -2 size","hp":114,"hd":"12d10+48","hdvalue":12,"fort":12,"ref":12,"will":8,"immunities":["gaze attacks","visual effects and illusions","sight-based attacks","sonic"],"weaknesses":["blind"],"speed":[{"type":"land","speed":20},{"type":"fly","speed":60,"maneuverability":"average"}],"melee":"bite +17 (2d6+7), 2 claws +17 (1d8+7)","ranged":"sonic lance +12 ranged touch (8d6 sonic)","space":"15 ft.","reach":"10 ft.","special_attacks":[{"type":"explosion"}],"strength":24,"dexterity":14,"constitution":18,"intelligence":7,"wisdom":15,"charisma":11,"baseatk":12,"cmb":21,"cmd":34,"cmd_special":"+4 vs. trip","feats":[{"feat":"Dodge"},{"feat":"Flyby Attack"},{"feat":"Improved Initiative"},{"feat":"Iron Will"},{"feat":"Lightning Reflexes"},{"feat":"Skill Focus (Perception)"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Fly","value":7},{"skill":"Perception","value":18}],"languages":["Draconic"],"environments":["any hills","any mountains","temperate deserts"],"organizations":["solitary","pair","clutch (3-6)"],"treasure":"incidental","description_visual":"This flying reptile has large, leathery wings and a vibrantly colored crest on its horned, narrow-snouted head.","source":"PFRPG Bestiary 2","special_abilities":[{"type":"Blind","kind":"Ex","details":"A yrthak sees and senses exclusively through its blindsight ability, which is based on sound and movement-beyond 120 ft., it is considered blind. A deaf yrthak is effectively blinded as well except against adjacent foes-its weak eyesight functions enough for it to attack targets this close, although in such cases these creatures still gain the benefit of concealment (20% miss chance) because of the creature's poor vision. It is invulnerable to all sight-based effects and attacks, including gaze attacks."},{"type":"Explosion","kind":"Ex","details":"As a standard action, a yrthak can fire its sonic lance at the ground, a large rock, a stone wall, or a similar nonmagical object within 60 ft. to create an explosion. This attack deals 2d6 points of piercing damage to all within 10 ft. of the effect's center."},{"type":"Sonic Lance","kind":"Ex","details":"Once per round, a yrthak can focus sonic energy in a 60-foot ray that deals 8d6 sonic damage to one target."}],"description":"Swift, cunning, and perpetually ravenous, the yrthak terrorizes the barren wastelands in which it makes its home, swooping down from on high to blast prey with bursts of pure sound. Though technically blind, as its eyes are tiny and barely capable of vision beyond a few ft., the yrthak senses its surroundings via acute hearing and echolocation. While its powerful jaws and claws are equally capable of taking down opponents, the yrthak generally prefers to wheel through the sky on its membranous wings, firing bolt after bolt of sound into its prey, and exulting in the thrill of the hunt. An adult yrthak is 20 ft. long and weighs 1,500 pounds.\n\nYrthaks spend most of their time aloft-a yrthak hunt often lasts several days, with the yrthak skimming roughly 100 ft. over the ground in its wide-ranging search for live prey, only resorting to grazing on carrion in direst need. While they have near-human intelligence, yrthaks generally don't seem interested in forming societies of their own-although the sight of a clutch of yrthaks tormenting a captured morsel might seem to indicate otherwise.","ecology":"","habitat_society":""},{"name":"Zelekhut","cr":9,"xp":6400,"alignment":"LN","size":"Large","type":"outsider","subtypes":["extraplanar","inevitable","lawful"],"init":9,"senses":[{"type":"darkvision","modifier":"60 ft."},{"type":"low-light vision"},{"type":"true seeing"}],"ac":24,"ac_touch":15,"ac_flat_footed":18,"ac_mods":"+5 Dex, +1 dodge, +9 natural, -1 size","hp":115,"hd":"10d10+60","hdvalue":10,"hp_mods":["regeneration 5 (chaotic)"],"fort":10,"ref":8,"will":10,"defensive_abilities":["constructed"],"dr":"10/chaotic","sr":20,"speed":[{"type":"land","speed":50},{"type":"fly","speed":60,"maneuverability":"average"}],"melee":"2 chains +17 (2d6+7 plus 1d6 electricity and trip)","space":"10 ft.","reach":"10 ft.","spell_like_abilities_caster_level":10,"spell_like_abilities_concentration":13,"spell_like_abilities":[{"frequency":"constant","spells":[{"spell":"true seeing"}]},{"frequency":"at-will","spells":[{"spell":"clairaudience/clairvoyance"},{"spell":"dimensional anchor"},{"spell":"dispel magic"},{"spell":"fear"},{"spell":"hold person"},{"spell":"locate creature"}]},{"frequency":"3/day","spells":[{"spell":"hold monster"},{"spell":"mark of justice"}]},{"frequency":"1/week","spells":[{"spell":"lesser geas"}]}],"strength":25,"dexterity":20,"constitution":16,"intelligence":10,"wisdom":17,"charisma":17,"baseatk":10,"cmb":18,"cmd":34,"cmd_special":"+4 vs. trip","feats":[{"feat":"Dodge"},{"feat":"Improved Initiative"},{"feat":"Mobility"},{"feat":"Weapon Focus (chain)"},{"feat":"Vital Strike"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Acrobatics","value":18,"special":"+26 jump"},{"skill":"Diplomacy","value":16},{"skill":"Fly","value":16},{"skill":"Perception","value":20},{"skill":"Sense Motive","value":20},{"skill":"Survival","value":16}],"languages":["truespeech"],"sq":[{"type":"chains"}],"environments":["any land (lawful plane)"],"organizations":["solitary"],"treasure":"none","description_visual":"This creature looks like a mechanical centaur. Golden, clockwork wings sprout from its back, and its arms end in barbed chains.","group":"Inevitable","source":"PFRPG Bestiary 2","special_abilities":[{"type":"Chains","kind":"Ex","details":"A zelekhut's arms end in long lengths of barbed metal. These chains deal slashing damage and 1d6 points of electricity damage with each hit."}],"description":"Zelekhuts are bounty hunters and executioners all rolled into one. They seek out those beings who continually evade justice-either through active flight, or through power and station-and bring law and justice to the multiverse's most notorious fugitives and criminals.\n\nIronically, while zelekhuts are implacable and unrelenting in their duty, they have little interest in passing judgment of their own, a fact that often confuses other races. Rather, a zelekhut is content to enforce the laws of any given society, and while it might hunt a condemned serial killer or notorious thief across half a dozen planes, it will not shift a single hoof to capture a corrupt ruler whose offenses are 10 times worse, so long as the atrocities are within her technical rights as ruler. All zelekhuts understand that laws can and must differ from place to place, and it isn't the zelekhut's job to moralize, merely to track down those who seek to flee their punishment.","ecology":"","habitat_society":""},{"name":"Zeuglodon","cr":9,"xp":6400,"alignment":"N","size":"Gargantuan","type":"animal","init":8,"senses":[{"type":"low-light vision"}],"ac":25,"ac_touch":11,"ac_flat_footed":20,"ac_mods":"+4 Dex, +1 dodge, +14 natural, -4 size","hp":115,"hd":"11d8+66","hdvalue":11,"fort":13,"ref":11,"will":6,"speed":[{"type":"swim","speed":60}],"melee":"bite +17 (2d8+19 plus grab)","space":"20 ft.","reach":"20 ft.","special_attacks":[{"type":"thrash"}],"strength":37,"dexterity":18,"constitution":22,"intelligence":1,"wisdom":13,"charisma":6,"baseatk":8,"cmb":25,"cmb_special":"+4 vs. grapple","cmd":40,"cmd_special":"can't be tripped","feats":[{"feat":"Dodge"},{"feat":"Improved Initiative"},{"feat":"Iron Will"},{"feat":"Lunge"},{"feat":"Power Attack"},{"feat":"Run"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Perception","value":20},{"skill":"Swim","value":27}],"sq":[{"type":"hold breath"}],"environments":["warm oceans"],"organizations":["solitary","pair"],"treasure":"none","description_visual":"This elongated, whale-like creature moves through the water with an eel-like motion despite its wide, fluked tail. Razor-sharp teeth fill its almost reptilian mouth.","source":"AP 60","special_abilities":[{"type":"Hold Breath","kind":"Ex","details":"A zeuglodon can hold its breath for a number of rounds equal to 4 times its Constitution score before it risks drowning."},{"type":"Thrash","kind":"Ex","details":"A zeuglodon grappling a foe can thrash its body back and forth rapidly, dealing extra damage due to the violent motion of its whipping head. This attack deals 4d8+19 points of damage, but allows the grappled creature a free attempt to escape the grapple. If a creature escapes, it is thrown 30 ft. in a random direction by the zeuglodon's erratic thrashing."}],"description":"The primordial zeuglodon is often mistaken for a dinosaur or other large reptile, in part because of its almost crocodilian mouth as well as its snake-like elongation. Despite these features, it is more closely related to whales and other cetaceans than either aquatic reptiles or fish. A zeuglodon moves through the water with a vertical anguiliform (eel-like) motion that seems almost to be a primitive version of the efficient fluke-driven locomotion of its cetacean relatives. Zeuglodons breathe air through blowholes on the tops of their heads, though they lack the lung capacity to stay underwater for as long as their more evolved kin. The relative dimensions of their angular heads are too small to encase the enlarged brains or melons developed by other cetaceans for echolocation or communication with others of their kind, and as such zeuglodons are less social than whales and dolphins. What they lack in specialized anatomy, however, they make up for in sheer ferocity and speed. A hunting zeuglodon is a furious foe to contend with. An adult zeuglodon measures around 50 ft. long and weighs upward of 50,000 pounds.","ecology":"","habitat_society":""},{"name":"Abaia","cr":10,"xp":9600,"alignment":"N","size":"Huge","type":"magical beast","subtypes":["aquatic"],"init":3,"senses":[{"type":"arcane sight"},{"type":"darkvision","modifier":"60 ft."},{"type":"low-light vision"}],"ac":25,"ac_touch":11,"ac_flat_footed":22,"ac_mods":"+3 Dex, +14 natural, -2 size","hp":147,"hd":"14d10+70","hdvalue":14,"fort":14,"ref":12,"will":8,"sr":21,"sr_mods":"in water only","speed":[{"type":"land","speed":20},{"type":"swim","speed":80}],"melee":"bite +21 (3d6+8/19-20 plus grab), tail slap +15 (2d6+4 plus grab)","space":"15 ft.","reach":"15 ft.","special_attacks":[{"type":"constrict","details":"2d6+12"},{"type":"endless coils"}],"spell_like_abilities_caster_level":14,"spell_like_abilities_concentration":19,"spell_like_abilities":[{"frequency":"constant","spells":[{"spell":"arcane sight"},{"spell":"speak with animals"}]},{"frequency":"at-will","spells":[{"spell":"control water"},{"spell":"hydraulic torrent"},{"spell":"rainbow pattern"}]},{"frequency":"1/day","spells":[{"spell":"control weather"}]}],"strength":26,"dexterity":16,"constitution":21,"intelligence":17,"wisdom":14,"charisma":17,"baseatk":14,"cmb":24,"cmb_special":"+4 vs. grapple","cmd":37,"cmd_special":"can't be tripped","feats":[{"feat":"Critical Focus"},{"feat":"Improved Critical (bite)"},{"feat":"Iron Will"},{"feat":"Power Attack"},{"feat":"Staggering Critical"},{"feat":"Vital Strike"},{"feat":"Weapon Focus (bite)"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Knowledge (arcana)","value":17},{"skill":"Knowledge (nature)","value":17},{"skill":"Perception","value":19},{"skill":"Spellcraft","value":17},{"skill":"Stealth","value":12,"special":"+24 in water"},{"skill":"Swim","value":16}],"languages":["Aquan","Sylvan","speak with animals"],"sq":[{"type":"eldritch gizzard"},{"type":"wave rider"}],"environments":["warm lakes"],"organizations":["solitary"],"treasure":"standard (particularly staves and wands)","description_visual":"This multi-eyed eel's brightly colored markings shift in complex, ever-changing patterns.","source":"PFRPG Bestiary 4","special_abilities":[{"type":"Eldritch Gizzard","kind":"Su","details":"An abaia can activate arcane spell trigger items as if it were a 14th-level sorcerer. It can store items in a special compartment within its stomach and activate them as if it were holding them. It can swallow or regurgitate an item as a standard action."},{"type":"Endless Coils","kind":"Ex","details":"As a full-round action, an abaia can attempt a single combat maneuver check to grapple up to two Large or four Medium or smaller creatures within its reach. Any targets successfully grabbed take constrict damage. The abaia only needs to succeed at one grapple check to maintain a grapple against multiple opponents."},{"type":"Wave Rider","kind":"Su","details":"An abaia moving onto land brings a sheath of water with it, allowing it to swim on land. Its swim speed drops by 10 ft. at the start of its turn if it is out of the water, and the sheath dissipates entirely when the abaia's swim speed reaches 20 ft. An abaia wave riding on land retains its spell resistance but loses its bonus to Stealth."}],"description":"Originally from the primal world of the fey, an abaia protects lakes and their surroundings from exploitation, in particular by magic and overfishing. It favors waters with a mystical nature or supernatural properties. An abaia ignores creatures that take only what they need from the lake and otherwise show proper respect to the waters. Those that abuse an abaia's lake risk capsized boats, floods, torrential rains, and even direct attacks. After sinking a vessel, an abaia searches the wreckage for magical treasure.","ecology":"","habitat_society":""},{"name":"Adlet","cr":10,"xp":9600,"alignment":"CN","size":"Medium","type":"humanoid","subtypes":["adlet","cold"],"init":12,"senses":[{"type":"low-light vision"},{"type":"scent"}],"ac":24,"ac_touch":19,"ac_flat_footed":15,"ac_mods":"+8 Dex, +1 dodge, +5 natural","hp":127,"hd":"15d8+60","hdvalue":15,"fort":9,"ref":17,"will":8,"immunities":["cold"],"weaknesses":["vulnerability to fire"],"speed":[{"type":"land","speed":40}],"melee":"+1 spear +17 (1d8+7/x3), bite +10 (1d6+2 plus 1d6 cold)","space":"5 ft.","reach":"5 ft.","special_attacks":[{"type":"frozen breath"}],"spell_like_abilities_caster_level":10,"spell_like_abilities_concentration":14,"spell_like_abilities":[{"frequency":"constant","spells":[{"spell":"pass without trace"}]},{"frequency":"at-will","spells":[{"spell":"ray of frost"}]},{"frequency":"1/day","spells":[{"spell":"ice storm"},{"spell":"wind walk","details":"self only"}]},{"frequency":"3/day","spells":[{"spell":"fog cloud"},{"spell":"sleet storm"}]}],"strength":18,"dexterity":26,"constitution":18,"intelligence":13,"wisdom":17,"charisma":13,"baseatk":11,"cmb":15,"cmd":35,"feats":[{"feat":"Diehard"},{"feat":"Dodge"},{"feat":"Endurance"},{"feat":"Improved Initiative"},{"feat":"Power Attack"},{"feat":"Run"},{"feat":"Self-Sufficient"},{"feat":"Weapon Focus (spear)"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Acrobatics","value":13,"special":"+17 when jumping"},{"skill":"Climb","value":12},{"skill":"Handle Animal","value":9},{"skill":"Heal","value":5},{"skill":"Perception","value":13},{"skill":"Stealth","value":13,"special":"+21 in snow"},{"skill":"Survival","value":20},{"skill":"Swim","value":9}],"languages":["Adlet","Common"],"sq":[{"type":"arctic stride"}],"environments":["cold plains","any hills","any mountains"],"organizations":["solitary","pair","pack (3-18 plus 1 shaman)"],"treasure":"standard (+1 spear)","description_visual":"This humanoid wolf 's fur is snowy white and its eyes piercing blue; it grips an ornate spear in its fist.","source":"PFRPG Bestiary 3","special_abilities":[{"type":"Arctic Stride","kind":"Ex","details":"An adlet can move through any sort of difficult terrain at its normal speed while within arctic or snowy terrain. Magically altered terrain affects an adlet normally."},{"type":"Frozen Breath","kind":"Su","details":"An adlet's breath is supernaturally cold, and deals an additional 1d6 points of cold damage with its bite. Once every 1d4 rounds as a swift action, it can exhale, filling a 10-footradius spread around it with frigid air that deals 2d6 points of cold damage and staggers those in the area with numbing cold for 1d6 rounds. A DC 21 Fortitude save negates the staggered effect but not the cold damage. The save DC is Constitution-based."}],"description":"Adlets are cunning hunters of the arctic wilds. Tall, sinewy, nimble, and very quick, they see themselves as the true heritors of untamed arctic lands, and are offended by any other humanoid species that attempts to settle in such regions. Although not normally evil, adlets are very aggressive and warlike. They also have no social taboo against cannibalism, and their practice of eating their dead rather than burying them only further builds misconceptions about their morality.\n\nDeeply religious, adlets worship the power and cruelty of nature, seeing divinity in the lash of the blizzard's wind, the ferocity of the polar bear, and the immensity of the towering iceberg. Many become oracles or druids, but all adlets know their place in the natural world. One in every dozen adlets is a shaman: an adlet with the advanced creature template and the ability to summon a greater ice elemental or 1d4+1 large ice elementals and commune with nature once per day each as spell-like abilities.\n\nAn adlet is 6 ft. tall and weighs 250 pounds.","ecology":"","habitat_society":""},{"name":"Adult Crystal Dragon","cr":10,"xp":9600,"alignment":"CG","size":"Large","type":"dragon","subtypes":["earth","extraplanar"],"init":1,"senses":[{"type":"dragon senses"},{"type":"tremorsense","modifier":"60 ft."}],"auras":["frightful presence (180 ft., DC 22)"],"ac":27,"ac_touch":10,"ac_flat_footed":26,"ac_mods":"+1 Dex, +17 natural, -1 size","hp":149,"hd":"13d12+65","hdvalue":13,"fort":15,"ref":11,"will":11,"dr":"5/magic","immunities":["paralysis","sleep","sonic"],"sr":21,"speed":[{"type":"land","speed":60},{"type":"burrow","speed":30},{"type":"climb","speed":30},{"type":"fly","speed":200,"maneuverability":"poor"}],"melee":"bite +19 (2d6+9/19-20), 2 claws +18 (1d8+6), tail slap +16 (1d8+9), 2 wings +16 (1d6+3)","space":"10 ft.","reach":"5 ft. (10 ft. with bite)","special_attacks":[{"type":"breath weapon","details":"40-ft. cone, 12d4 sonic, DC 21"}],"spell_like_abilities_caster_level":13,"spell_like_abilities_concentration":18,"spell_like_abilities":[{"frequency":"at-will","spells":[{"spell":"color spray"},{"spell":"glitterdust"},{"spell":"rainbow pattern"}]}],"spellsknown_caster_level":1,"spellsknown_concentration":6,"spellsknown":[{"spell_level":1,"spell_slots":5,"spells":[{"spell":"shield"},{"spell":"unseen servant"}]},{"spell_level":0,"spell_slots":99,"spells":[{"spell":"acid splash"},{"spell":"detect magic"},{"spell":"ghost sound"},{"spell":"read magic"}]}],"strength":23,"dexterity":12,"constitution":21,"intelligence":16,"wisdom":17,"charisma":22,"baseatk":13,"cmb":20,"cmd":31,"cmd_special":"+4 vs. trip","feats":[{"feat":"Deceitful"},{"feat":"Great Fortitude"},{"feat":"Improved Critical (bite)"},{"feat":"Lightning Reflexes"},{"feat":"Multiattack"},{"feat":"Power Attack"},{"feat":"Weapon Focus (bite)"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Bluff","value":26},{"skill":"Climb","value":30},{"skill":"Disguise","value":23},{"skill":"Fly","value":11},{"skill":"Intimidate","value":22},{"skill":"Knowledge (dungeoneering)","value":19},{"skill":"Perception","value":19},{"skill":"Sense Motive","value":19},{"skill":"Stealth","value":13}],"languages":["Common","Draconic","Terran","Undercommon"],"sq":[{"type":"razor sharp"}],"environments":["any underground (Plane of Earth)"],"organizations":["solitary"],"treasure":"triple","description_visual":"This brilliantly colored dragon has scales, teeth, and claws made of multicolored crystal, and its wings are sheets of flexible glass.","group":"Primal Dragon","source":"PFRPG Bestiary 2","special_abilities":[{"type":"Razor Sharp","kind":"Sp","details":"All of a crystal dragon's natural attacks deal slashing damage."},{"type":"Ray Reflection","kind":"Ex","details":"An ancient crystal dragon's scales reflect ray spells back upon the ray's source if the ray fails to overcome the dragon's spell resistance."},{"type":"Scintillating Aura","kind":"Su","details":"A great wyrm crystal dragon radiates an aura of scintillating color from its jeweled scales to a radius of 60 ft. All within this area must make a Will save each round to avoid being stunned (if the victim has 15 or fewer Hit Dice) or confused (if the victim has more than 15 Hit Dice) for 1 round. The save DC is equal to the dragon's breath weapon save DC. This is a mind-affecting effect. The dragon can activate or suppress this aura as a free action."},{"type":"Spell-Like Abilities","kind":"Sp","details":"A crystal dragon gains the following spell-like abilities, usable at will (unless indicated otherwise) upon reaching the listed age category. Very young-color spray; Juvenile-glitterdust; Adult-rainbow pattern; Old- stone to flesh (3/day); Ancient-prismatic spray (3/day); Great wyrm-imprisonment (1/day)."},{"type":"Tremorsense","kind":"Ex","details":"Crystal dragons don't gain tremorsense until juvenile age (30 ft.), improving at adult (60 ft.) and old (120 ft.)."}],"description":"Crystal dragons are generally good-natured, though their incredible vanity sometimes causes them to seem aloof and cocky. Any perceived insult against its appearance is all but assured to send a crystal dragon into a rage-which is a problem, as most crystal dragons are prone to seeing insults even where none are intended. Crystal dragons prefer underground lairs, and often go for decades or even centuries without emerging from their extensive cavern lairs onto the surface world above.\n\nCrystal dragons tend to be exacting and even obsessive-compulsive, their personalities mirroring the precise and ordered nature of the facets of their scales. A crystal dragon's lair is a well-ordered place-these dragons find the very idea of the classic sprawl of a dragon's hoard to be shameful.","ecology":"","habitat_society":""},{"name":"Adult White Dragon","cr":10,"xp":9600,"alignment":"CE","size":"Large","type":"dragon","subtypes":["cold"],"init":5,"senses":[{"type":"dragon senses"},{"type":"snow vision"}],"auras":["cold (5 ft., 1d6 cold damage)","frightful presence (180 ft., DC 17)"],"ac":27,"ac_touch":10,"ac_flat_footed":26,"ac_mods":"+1 Dex, +17 natural, -1 size","hp":149,"hd":"13d12+65","hdvalue":13,"fort":13,"ref":9,"will":10,"dr":"5/magic","immunities":["cold","paralysis","sleep"],"sr":21,"weaknesses":["vulnerability to fire"],"speed":[{"type":"land","speed":30},{"type":"burrow","speed":30},{"type":"fly","speed":200,"maneuverability":"poor"},{"type":"swim","speed":60}],"melee":"bite +20 (2d6+10/19-20), 2 claws +19 (1d8+7), 2 wings +14 (1d6+3), tail slap +14 (1d8+10)","space":"10 ft.","reach":"5 ft. (10 ft. with bite)","special_attacks":[{"type":"breath weapon","details":"40-ft. cone, DC 21, 12d4 cold"}],"spell_like_abilities_caster_level":13,"spell_like_abilities_concentration":18,"spell_like_abilities":[{"frequency":"at-will","spells":[{"spell":"fog cloud"},{"spell":"gust of wind"}]}],"spellsknown_caster_level":1,"spellsknown_concentration":6,"spellsknown":[{"spell_level":1,"spell_slots":4,"spells":[{"spell":"shield"},{"spell":"true strike"}]},{"spell_level":0,"spell_slots":99,"spells":[{"spell":"dancing lights"},{"spell":"detect magic"},{"spell":"ray of frost"},{"spell":"mending"}]}],"strength":25,"dexterity":12,"constitution":21,"intelligence":12,"wisdom":15,"charisma":12,"baseatk":13,"cmb":21,"cmd":32,"cmd_special":"+4 vs. trip","feats":[{"feat":"Alertness"},{"feat":"Flyby Attack"},{"feat":"Improved Critical (bite)"},{"feat":"Improved Initiative"},{"feat":"Power Attack"},{"feat":"Vital Strike"},{"feat":"Weapon Focus (bite)"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Fly","value":11},{"skill":"Intimidate","value":17},{"skill":"Knowledge (arcane)","value":17},{"skill":"Perception","value":22},{"skill":"Spellcraft","value":17},{"skill":"Stealth","value":13},{"skill":"Swim","value":31}],"languages":["Common","Draconic"],"sq":[{"type":"icewalking"},{"type":"ice shape"}],"environments":["cold mountains"],"organizations":["solitary"],"treasure":"triple","description_visual":"This dragon's scales are a frosty white. Its head is crowned with slender horns, with a thin membrane stretched between them.","group":"Chromatic Dragon","source":"PFRPG Bestiary","special_abilities":[{"type":"Blizzard","kind":"Su","details":"An ancient white dragon can use its breath weapon to create a blizzard in the area around it as a standard action. This creates heavy snow conditions in a 50-foot radius for 1 minute, centered on the dragon. This snow slows movement (4 squares of movement per square entered) and limits vision as fog does."},{"type":"Cold Aura","kind":"Su","details":"An adult white dragon radiates an aura of cold. All creatures within 5 ft. of the dragon take 1d6 points of cold damage at the beginning of the dragon's turn. An old dragon's aura extends to 10 ft. An ancient dragon's damage increases to 2d6."},{"type":"Freezing Fog","kind":"Sp","details":"An old white dragon can use this ability three times per day. It is similar to an acid fog spell but deals cold damage instead of acid damage. It also causes a rime of slippery ice to form on any surface the fog touches, creating the effect of a grease spell. The dragon is immune to the grease effect because of its icewalking ability. This ability is the equivalent of a 6th-level spell."},{"type":"Ice Shape","kind":"Su","details":"A young white dragon can shape ice and snow at will. This ability functions as stone shape, but only targeting ice and snow, not stone. A white dragon's caster level for this effect is equal to its Hit Dice."},{"type":"Ice Tomb","kind":"Sp","details":"A great wyrm can, as a standard action, cause a creature to sink into ice. This works as imprisonment, but only while the target is touching an icy surface. A white dragon can use this ability once per day (CL equals dragon's HD). Targets entombed by this ability can be freed by casting freedom or by physically freeing the creature from the ice (Hardness 0, 360 hit points). The save DC is Charisma-based."},{"type":"Icewalking","kind":"Ex","details":"This ability works like the spider climb spell, but the surfaces the dragon climbs must be icy. The dragon can move across icy surfaces without penalty and doesn't need to make Acrobatics checks to run or charge on ice."},{"type":"Snow Vision","kind":"Ex","details":"A very young white dragon learns to see perfectly well in snowy conditions. A white dragon doesn't suffer any penalties to Perception checks while in snow."},{"type":"Spell-Like Abilities","kind":"Sp","details":"A white dragon gains the following spell-like abilities usable at will upon reaching the listed age category. Juvenile-fog cloud; Young adult-gust of wind; Ancient-wall of ice; Great wyrm-control weather. Age Category S pecial Abilities Caster Level Wyrmling Icewalking, cold subtype - Very young Snow vision - Young Ice shape - Juvenile Fog cloud - Young adult DR 5/magic, spell resistance, - gust of wind Adult Cold aura, frightful presence 1st Mature adult DR 10/magic 3rd Old Freezing fog 5th Very old DR 15/magic 7th Ancient Blizzard, wall of ice 9th Wyrm DR 20/magic 11th Great wyrm Ice tomb, control weather 13th."}],"description":"Although most consider it to be the weakest and most feral of the chromatic dragons, the white dragon makes up for its lack of cunning with sheer ferocity. White dragons dwell on remote, frozen mountaintops and in arctic lowlands, making their home in glittering caves full of ice and snow. They prefer their meals completely frozen.","ecology":"","habitat_society":""}];
